---
name: invoice-email
description: Invoice e-mail whose body is rendered to PDF via the OPT-IN pdf provider
# `std.pdf` lives in an EXPLICIT, OPT-IN provider: build.sbt stages
# v2/runtime/providers/pdf-plugin under bin/lib/providers/pdf and its renderer deps
# (PDFBox, openhtmltopdf, jsoup) "never enter the standard launcher graph". So this case
# runs under `bin/ssc-provider pdf run` and under the v1 interpreter, and CANNOT run under
# `bin/ssc` / emit-js / run-jvm. Measured 2026-07-29: int=ok, js/jvm/v2=fail, and
# `bin/ssc-provider pdf run` renders at rc=0. Declaring the lanes stops the corpus contract
# counting a deliberate packaging boundary as a v2 defect (BUGS v2-optin-provider-cases).
backends: [int]
---

# Invoice email

```scalascript
import std.pdf.*
import std.mime.*

// The relay-free invoice email: render the invoice HTML to a PDF, then assemble
// a multipart/mixed message with the PDF attached — ready for an SMTP DATA send.

val invoiceHtml =
  "<html><head><style>" +
    "body{font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;margin:24px}" +
    "table{width:100%;border:1px solid #333;border-collapse:collapse}" +
    "th,td{padding:6px;border:1px solid #333}" +
    "</style></head><body>" +
    "<h1>Faktura FV/2026/1</h1>" +
    "<table><thead><tr><th>Pozycja</th><th>Kwota</th></tr></thead>" +
    "<tbody><tr><td>Usluga A</td><td>1000.01 zl</td></tr></tbody></table>" +
    "</body></html>"

val pdfBase64 = htmlToPdfBase64(invoiceHtml)

val message = buildMimeMessage(
  "billing@acme.example",
  "klient@example.com",
  "Faktura FV/2026/1",
  "<html><body><p>W zalaczniku faktura.</p></body></html>",
  List(("faktura-FV-2026-1.pdf", "application/pdf", pdfBase64))
)

if message.length > 0 then
  println("MIME message assembled: PDF attached")
else
  println("MIME message assembly failed")
```
